'''Jempa''' was a [[Whiphid]] member of [[Bear Clan]], a group of [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] within the [[Jedi Order]]. In [[22 BBY]], Jempa and the rest of the clan were given a lesson on [[lightsaber]] use by [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] interrupted the lesson to ask Yoda about a [[Kamino|planet]] he could not find in the [[Jedi Archives]] and was greeted by Jempa and the other [[youngling]]s.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Reach out. Sense the Force around you. Use your feelings you must.|Yoda instructs Jempa and the rest of Bear Clan|audio=Yoda-ReachOut.flac|<ref name="AOTC" />}}
Jempa was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Whiphid]]<ref name="AOTC" /> born at some point between around [[30 BBY]] and [[26 BBY]].<ref name="Date" /> The Whiphid was inducted into the [[Jedi Order]] and taken to the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] for [[Jedi training|training]].<ref name="AOTC" /> In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> Jempa was one of two Whiphid members<ref name="AOTC" /> of the [[Bear Clan]], a class of [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] all aged between four and eight [[Standard year|years]] old.<ref name="Bear Clan" /> During a class taught by [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]], Jempa and the rest of Bear Clan donned<ref name="AOTC" /> [[WJ-880 blinding helmet|youngling helmets]] that blocked their vision. This helped them to see using [[the Force]] rather than with their bodily senses alone while learning to sense [[blaster]] bolts fired by [[remote]]s and block them with [[training lightsaber]]s.<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

[[File:GreetingsMasterObiWan-AOTC.png|thumb|left|300px|Jempa and the other younglings greeted Obi-Wan Kenobi when he interrupted their training session in the Jedi Temple.]]
The lesson was interrupted by the arrival of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], which caused Yoda to pause and have Jempa and the other [[youngling]]s greet the visitor in unison. Kenobi returned the greeting and then explained to Yoda that he was searching for a [[Kamino|planet]] that he could not find in the [[Jedi Archives]]. Yoda joked that losing a planet must be embarrassing for Kenobi, eliciting a giggle from the younglings. He then had them all gather around the room's map reader, from which Kenobi projected a [[Hologram|holographic]] [[star map]] and showed where the planet ought to be. After Jempa's classmate [[J. K. Burtola]] suggested someone had erased the planet from the archives, Yoda instructed Kenobi to seek the world out.<ref name="AOTC" />

==Personality and traits==
Jempa had [[Color|gray]] skin and blue [[eye]]s.<ref name="AOTC" />

==Equipment==
While in class, Jempa wore brown [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] with a tan [[Clothing|shirt]] and pants underneath. The Whiphid also wore a brown [[belt]] and [[boot]]s and used a gray training [[helmet]] and a green [[lightsaber|training lightsaber]].<ref name="AOTC" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|He's not allowed to use the Force!''"<br />"''I acted on impulse. I didn't mean to.|The Togruta and Jempa in "Jedi Soccer"|<ref name="Soccer">{{StoryCite|story=Jedi Soccer|book=LEGO Star Wars: Galactic Freedom Fighters}}</ref>}}
Jempa appeared in the [[2002]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="AOTC" /> The character was portrayed by a child actor with digital effects used to add the [[alien]] head and hands,<ref name="Twitter1">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1490131317228376066|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2022-02-05|quote=The three non-human younglings are human performers with digital head and hand replacements. The Togruta girl is Ashla; the boy in the middle is a Whiphid named Jempa, and the Nikto on the right is Chian.|archivedate=20220206011755|nolive=1}}</ref> as well as the helmet.<ref name="Twitter2">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1490135977657974785|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2022-02-06|quote=Yes. The helmets and heads are modeled together.|archivedate=20220206093515|nolive=1}}</ref> Stunt coordinator [[Nick Gillard]] oversaw the casting call for actors to play the younglings on [[July 7]], [[2000]], after which the scenes in the Jedi Temple were shot on [[July 20]], 2000, in [[Fox Studios, Sydney]].<ref name="Archives">''[[The Star Wars Archives: Episodes I–III, 1999–2005]]''</ref> In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the character was identified in an entry for the Bear Clan in the [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]].<ref name="Bear Clan" /> The name was first used in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it appeared on packaging for a figure of Jempa released in [[2003]] by [[Hasbro]] as part of the [[Star Wars (Hasbro toy line)|''Star Wars Saga'']] toy line.<ref name="Toy">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars (Hasbro toy line)|packtype='03 Basic Figure|pack=#16: Ashla & Jempa (Jedi Padwans)|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/sw0316ashlajempa.asp}}</ref>

[[File:LEGOSoccer.png|thumb|250px|right|Jempa (second from the left) plays soccer with other younglings.]]
In "[[Jedi Soccer]]," a non-canon comic short published in the [[2015]] activity book ''[[LEGO Star Wars: Galactic Freedom Fighters]]'', he/him pronouns are used for Jempa. In the comic, he is shown playing goalie in a game of [[soccer]] with a group of other Jedi [[Padawan]]s. A [[Unidentified Nautolan Padawan (LEGO)|Nautolan]] Padawan kicks the ball at Jempa, who then breaks the rules by using the Force to stop it in mid air. A [[Unidentified Togruta Padawan (LEGO)|Togruta]] Padawan complains at the Whiphid's use of the Force, but Jempa claims that it was unintential as he was acting on impulse. The [[Togruta]] and the [[Nautolan]] then joke that the Force is preferable to Jempa using a lightsaber as the Whipid is sick of having to buy new balls.<ref name="Soccer" />

